    <string name="terminal_cortex_enabled">Use Cortex for Linux (experimental)</string>
    <string name="terminal_cortex_details">Cortex compatibility details</string>
    <string name="terminal_cortex_warning">PRoot remains the default. This switch affects new Linux commands only. Cortex needs its own compatible runtime; ordinary Linux images are not supported. It is not a sandbox or a complete Linux kernel. Android may deny execution from app storage, especially with target API 29 or later (AIDE+ targets 34). No root, SDK downgrade or silent fallback is used. Import a trusted runtime, select the imported instance, then enable this option to try; turn it off to return to PRoot.</string>
