    <string name="terminal_root_chroot_enabled">Root chroot Linux (experimental)</string>
    <string name="terminal_root_chroot_warning">Only for rooted devices with explicit su authorization. This disables Cortex; both off uses PRoot. Requires working mount/PID namespaces, unshare, mount, chroot, find and chown (usually root BusyBox). Mounts remain private; unsupported tools or SELinux restrictions cause an error, never a fallback or SELinux changes. Linux commands run as real root: chroot is NOT a security sandbox or a VM. On normal exit, ownership of this private rootfs is returned to the app UID; forced process kills may need manual recovery. Close all Linux sessions before switching. No guarantee of systemd or kernel compatibility. Continue?</string>
